{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>in all your settlements</b> — This teaches that the Sanhedrin functions outside the Land so long as it functions in the Land of Israel; this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 35:29). And so it is, for after the Destruction it functions neither in the Land of Israel nor outside the Land, as our Rabbis said in the chapter \"Four Modes of Execution\" (Sanhedrin 52a): \"And you shall come to the priests the Levites and to the judge who shall be in those days\" (Deuteronomy 17:9) — when there is a priest there is justice, when there is no priest there is no justice. And they taught in the Mekhilta: From where do we know that they execute only when the Temple stands? For it is stated: \"from My altar you shall take him to die\" (Exodus 21:14) — if you have an altar you execute, and if not you do not execute. But I have not found in a commandment that depends on the time of the Temple that it says concerning it \"for your generations in all your settlements,\" for this expression indicates even the time of exile outside the Land, as is stated regarding the festival of Shavuot (Leviticus 23:21) and regarding the prohibition of the new grain (ibid. v. 14), to obligate them outside the Land at this time, since He did not make that dependent on the omer and the new meal-offering, and likewise regarding forbidden fat (ibid. 3:17), which He did not make dependent on the offerings. But perhaps they interpret \"these shall be for you a statute of judgment\" as referring to the Sanhedrin mentioned throughout the passage, as it is stated \"before the congregation for judgment\" (Numbers 35:12), \"and the congregation shall judge\" (Numbers 35:24), and He says that there shall be for us for all generations a congregation that judges even after the Destruction, to adjudicate cases of fines and robbery and injuries and all monetary matters and lashes of forty."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:10:26.368886307Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}